==Bavarian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|bar|heifa||West Central}}
* {{alt|bar|hölfn||Southern}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bar|gmh|helfen|hëlfen}}, from {{inh|bar|goh|helfan}}, from {{inh|bar|gmw-pro|*helpan}}, from {{inh|bar|gem-pro|*helpaną}}, from {{der|bar|ine-pro|[[*ḱelb-]], [[*ḱelp-]]}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|helfen}}, {{cog|nds|helpen}}, {{cog|nl|helpen}}, {{cog|en|help}}, {{cog|da|hjælpe}}, {{cog|nb|hjelpe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|bar|/ˈhœːfɱ̩/}}
* {{hyphenation|bar|höfn}}

===Verb===
{{bar-verb|pp=ghoifn}} {{tlb|bar|East Central|Vienna}}

# {{lb|bar|intransitive}} to [[help]] (someone); to [[assist]]; to [[aid]]
#: {{uxi|bar|Kå ma wer '''höfn''', bittschee?|Can someone '''help''' me, please?.}}
#: {{uxi|bar|Des Mittl då '''hüft''' gegn Kopfweh.|This product '''helps''' to relieve headaches.}}

